{
  "dom_id": "step-q174368",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A={2,4,8}$ of $X={0,2,4,6,8}.$",
  "worked_solution": "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set ${2,4,8}$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114807/assets/850019897d92b0a8d3340c091cee15342be20e99e7578a9fca23f88804e3bf28.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $2,4$ and $8$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
